# An ordinary rig project ignores generated code — see the .gitignore that
# `rig init` writes. This example commits it on purpose: CI runs `rig check`
# here and writes nothing, so any drift between the schema, the generators and
# what is committed shows up as a failure and then as a diff in review, rather
# than as a surprise later. `make update-examples` is what regenerates it.

# rig's working directory.
.rig/manifest.json

# Binaries
/bin/
